# A cold and dark aeroplane that nobody has touched: its lights read off and
# its battery is not known at all - which, now that X-Plane's generic battery
# is no longer read, is how almost every aeroplane loads.
#
# Caught live in September 2026 on four aeroplanes at once. The generic battery,
# sim/cockpit2/electrical/battery_on[0], read 1 on a cold ToLiss A320, a King
# Air 350 and a LevelUp 737, and 0 on Laminar's own 737 - the only one of the
# four that stayed quiet. The LevelUp was the telling one: its own nav,
# landing, taxi and logo all said "off", the stock battery said "on", and "any
# one of the four is awake" took the battery's word. Boarding was announced in
# a cockpit nobody had powered.
#
# What the bench can check is the consequence, not the binding. It has no
# dataref layer: the battery comes in here as unknown and the lights as off,
# already decided. Whether the plugin really binds that way on a given
# aeroplane is only visible in the simulator, on the Triggers tab.

config auto_boarding=1 boarding_music=0
library BoardingStarted BoardingWelcome

set hour=12 on_ground=1 engines=0 gs_kt=0
set battery=unknown nav=0 taxi=0 logo=0
set beacon=0 strobe=0 landing=0 parkbrake=1 seatbelt=unknown

# ---- while the aeroplane's own datarefs are still being looked for ---------
advance 20
expect phase PREFLIGHT
expect not-played BoardingStarted

# ---- and after the search has given up ------------------------------------
# The wave-through is for an aeroplane that publishes none of the four. This
# one publishes three, and all three say off: an unknown battery next to them
# is not a reason to open the cabin.
advance 150
expect phase PREFLIGHT
expect not-played BoardingStarted
expect not-played BoardingWelcome

# ---- the crew wakes the aeroplane up --------------------------------------
# The positive control: without it, a machine that never boards at all would
# pass everything above.
set nav=1
advance 10
expect phase BOARDING
expect played BoardingStarted
